<title>USA: U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boxed beef generally lower on good demand and heavy offerings. Select and Choice chuck and round cuts weak, while loin cuts lower and rib cuts mostly steady. Beef trimming steady on light to moderate demand and offerings. - USDA</p>
<p>-----</p>
<p>445 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p> 20 50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>28 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     102.11	101.19	 95.64	 94.87</p>
<p>Changes	  -0.65	 -0.81	 -0.72	 -0.78</p>
<p>Rib	  159.89	158.19	150.01	149.62</p>
<p>Chuck	 68.86	 66.23	 68.13	 65.13</p>
<p>Round	 86.09	 86.09	 83.17	 83.17</p>
<p>Loin	 168.44	168.65	147.28	148.08</p>
<p>Brisket     56.91	 56.91	 56.70	 56.70</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  60.03	 59.96	 60.23	 60.09</p>
<p>Flank	 55.95	 55.95	 54.74	 54.74</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
